        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Alamorio, Imperial County, California, Alamo River, North America, Europe, western Asia\n- Concepts: unincorporated communities, place names, Spanish word origins, species native ranges\n- Biological taxa: Populus sect. Aigeiros\n\nFacts:\n- Alamorio is an unincorporated community in Imperial County, California.\n- Alamorio is located along the Alamo River.\n- Alamorio was named by combining the Spanish words \"alamo,\" meaning \"poplar\" or \"cottonwood,\" and \"rio,\" meaning \"river.\"\n- The species in Populus sect. Aigeiros are native to North America, Europe, and western Asia.",
